# WHAT LEAVES THIS MACHINE.
#
# An sdist is permanent and public, and setuptools' defaults are generous: it
# sweeps in `tests/` and the repository root README. This package lives in a
# multi-project research repository, so both defaults shipped material from
# unrelated work -- 30 foreign test files, and a root README describing another
# system and naming a private repository.
#
# So the default is inverted here: prune, then name what ships. The PyPI page
# is built from trustband/README.md (see `readme` in pyproject.toml); the root
# README is not needed to build or install and does not go out.
prune tests
include tests/test_claude_code_adapter.py
include tests/test_mcp_proxy.py
include tests/test_tool_descriptions.py
include tests/test_extractor_core.py

exclude README.md
exclude setup.cfg
